  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n2 (1)/(2)+3(1)/(2)+4(1)/(2)=x,\n\nWe need to find x - 5(1)/(2).\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nStep 1: Convert mixed fractions to improper fractions:\n\n2 (1)/(2) = (5)/(2), 3 (1)/(2) = (7)/(2), 4 (1)/(2) = (9)/(2)\n\nStep 2: Add the fractions:\n\nx = (5)/(2) + (7)/(2) + (9)/(2)\n\n⇒ x = ((5 + 7 + 9))/(2) = (21)/(2) = 10 (1)/(2)\n\nStep 3: Subtract 5 (1)/(2) from x:\n\nx - 5 (1)/(2) = 10 (1)/(2) - 5 (1)/(2)\n\n⇒ x - 5 (1)/(2) = (10 - 5) + ((1)/(2) - (1)/(2)) = 5\n\n**∴ The value of x - 5 (1)/(2) is 5.**",
